  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(a) Ethyl chioride gives ethyl cyanide, when it reacts with KCN (ethanolic).\r\n$$\r\n\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{KCN} \\stackrel{\\text { EThande }}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{C}_{2}\\mathrm{H}_{\\mathrm{s}}-\\mathrm{CN}\r\n$$\r\n(b) It does not react with KCN.\r\n(c) Benzaldehyde : KCN gives HCN in alcoholic medium and HCN gives cyanohydrin with benzaldehyde.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_che_a40.png\">",
